---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Icon from '../components/Icon.astro';
import CopyButton from '../components/CopyButton.astro';
import CodeBlock from '../components/CodeBlock.astro';
import {
  BOOTNODES,
  BOOTNODES_CSV,
  isTestnetLive,
  TESTNET_RPC_URL,
  TESTNET_CHAIN_ID,
  TESTNET_NODE_RELEASE,
} from '../config/testnet';

const joinPeer = `export BOING_CHAIN_ID=${TESTNET_CHAIN_ID}
./boing-node \\
  --data-dir ./boing-data \\
  --p2p-listen /ip4/0.0.0.0/tcp/4001 \\
  --bootnodes ${BOOTNODES_CSV} \\
  --rpc-port 8545`;
---

<Layout
  title="Bootnodes"
  description="How to use the official Boing Network testnet bootnode to join chain 6913."
>
  <article class="page-wrap-full">
    <header class="page-hero-full">
      <div class="page-wrap-inner">
        <span class="stage-badge-global">Testnet · chain {TESTNET_CHAIN_ID}</span>
        <h1 class="page-title"><Icon name="network" size={32} class="title-icon" /> Bootnodes</h1>
        <p class="lead">
          A <strong>bootnode</strong> is a stable peer your node dials first so it can find the rest of the network.
          Without one, a new node only discovers peers on the same local network.
        </p>
      </div>
    </header>
    <div class="page-wrap-inner bootnodes-content">
    <section class="section">
      <h2>In plain language</h2>
      <ol>
        <li>You start <code>boing-node</code> with <code>--p2p-listen</code> so other nodes can talk to you.</li>
        <li>You pass <code>--bootnodes</code> with the official address below.</li>
        <li>Your node connects, learns other peers, and syncs blocks for chain <strong>{TESTNET_CHAIN_ID}</strong>.</li>
      </ol>
      <p>Public JSON-RPC for apps stays at <code>{TESTNET_RPC_URL}</code> — you do not need to expose RPC to join as a peer.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="section" id="official">
      <h2>Official bootnode (live)</h2>
      {isTestnetLive && BOOTNODES.length > 0 ? (
        <>
          <p>
            Hosted on Fly <code>boing-testnet-1</code> only. The former companion
            <code>/ip4/109.105.220.118/tcp/4001</code> (<code>boing-testnet-2</code>) was <strong>retired 2026-10-24</strong> — do not dial it.
          </p>
          {BOOTNODES.map((bn) => (
            <div class="copy-wrapper rpc-copy" data-copy-value={bn}>
              <code class="rpc-url-display">{bn}</code>
              <CopyButton label="Copy" copiedLabel="Copied!" />
            </div>
          ))}
          <p class="muted small-print">
            Same value in <a href="/api/networks">/api/networks</a>,
            <a href="/pdfs/TESTNET.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener">TESTNET (PDF)</a>, and
            <a href="https://github.com/Boing-Network/boing.network/blob/main/docs/TESTNET.md" target="_blank" rel="noopener">docs/TESTNET.md</a>.
            Use release <strong>{TESTNET_NODE_RELEASE}</strong> or newer.
          </p>
        </>
      ) : (
        <p>Bootnode multiaddrs will appear here when the public testnet endpoints are configured.</p>
      )}
    </section>

    <section class="section">
      <h2>Copy-paste: join as a peer</h2>
      {isTestnetLive ? (
        <>
          <p>After you download or build <code>boing-node</code> (see <a href="/testnet/join#run-a-node">Join Testnet</a>):</p>
          <CodeBlock code={joinPeer} label="Join the public testnet" />
          <p>
            Open inbound <strong>TCP 4001</strong> if you want others to dial you.
            To become a <strong>validator</strong> (100 BOING bond), follow the
            <a href="/testnet/operators/validator">validator guide</a> — do not enable <code>--faucet-enable</code> on a community node.
          </p>
        </>
      ) : (
        <p>When public bootnodes are published, a copy-paste command will appear here.</p>
      )}
    </section>

    <section class="section">
      <h2>Local-only practice</h2>
      <p>On one machine: start node A with <code>--p2p-listen /ip4/127.0.0.1/tcp/4001</code>, then start node B with <code>--bootnodes /ip4/127.0.0.1/tcp/4001</code>. That does not join the public testnet.</p>
    </section>

    <nav class="section nav-links">
      <a href="/testnet/join">← Join Testnet</a>
      <a href="/testnet/operators/validator">Run a validator →</a>
    </nav>
    </div>
  </article>
</Layout>

<style>
  .bootnodes-content { padding-bottom: 3rem; }
  .page-title { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 0.5rem; color: var(--text-primary); }
  .title-icon { color: var(--accent-teal); flex-shrink: 0; }
  .bootnodes-content h1 { color: var(--text-primary); }
  .lead { color: var(--text-secondary); font-size: 1.1rem; }
  .section { margin-top: 2rem; }
  .section h2 { font-size: 1.25rem; color: var(--text-primary); margin-bottom: 0.5rem; }
  .section p, .section li { color: var(--text-secondary); }
  .section code { background: rgba(255,255,255,0.08); padding: 0.15rem 0.4rem; border-radius: 4px; font-size: 0.9em; }
  .section ol { margin: 0.5rem 0 0 1.2rem; }
  .muted { color: var(--text-secondary); font-size: 0.9rem; }
  .small-print { font-size: 0.85rem; margin-top: 0.5rem; }
  .rpc-copy {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 0.5rem;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    margin: 0.35rem 0;
  }
  .rpc-copy .rpc-url-display {
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    padding: 0.35rem 0.5rem;
    background: rgba(0,0,0,0.25);
    border-radius: 6px;
  }
  .nav-links { display: flex; justify-content: space-between; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 1rem; }
  .nav-links a { color: var(--accent-teal); font-weight: 500; }
  @media (max-width: 640px) {
    .bootnodes-content { padding-bottom: 2rem; }
    .section { margin-top: 1.5rem; }
  }
</style>
